course: dictionary
lesson: 8041
title: The word region
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A region is a large area of land or of a country, with its own features, such as its weather, plants or people. Geography lessons use the word a lot, as in polar regions and desert regions. Read the words around it for clues: «In a federation, states or regions run some things and the national government runs others.» Here regions are parts of a country that have some power of their own.
explain: The words after region can help too. «Marmots came back in reserves in the Luhansk and Kharkiv regions.» Those names tell you that a region is a named part of a bigger place, with its own position on the map.
explain: Region has other meanings as well. In maths, a region is one area or space on a diagram, such as a part of a Venn diagram. On the body, the lower back region is the part of your back near the bottom. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A region is a large area of land or of a country with its own features.
fact: «The Shandong region» is a part of China, so a region can be a part of a bigger country.
fact: «In the region of 100» means about 100.
fact: In a Venn diagram, each region is one part of the diagram where a group of numbers or things sits.
fact: Region can also mean a part of the body, such as the lower back region.
exercise: «Marmots came back in reserves in the Luhansk and Kharkiv regions.» What is a region here? | A small pond in a garden | A sail on a ship | *A large area of land with its own features | A kind of marmot food
exercise: Ella sorts numbers on a Venn diagram. What is each region on the diagram? | *An area or space on the diagram | A kind of sum that is always wrong | A ruler mark | A type of number
exercise: «The population was in the region of 100.» What does «in the region of» mean? | A line on a map | Less than 5 | *About 100 | Exactly 1,000
test: «In a federation, states or regions run some things.» In this sentence, what does regions mean? | A kind of weather | A maths diagram | *Parts of a country that run some things | A type of plant that grows in deserts
test: Which phrase uses region to mean a part of the body? | *The lower back region | The desert regions | The polar regions | A region of a Venn diagram
exam: In «New Zealand is named after the Dutch region of Zeeland», what is Zeeland? | A sea animal | *An area of land in the Netherlands | A maths sum | A type of sheep
